<title>USA: Ciena Corp hikes IPO pricing range.</title>
<headline>Ciena Corp hikes IPO pricing range.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecommunication components maker Ciena Corp has raised the price for shares of its red-hot initial public offering, according to underwriter Goldman Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The five million shares, which were originally set to price between $17 and $19 each, are now to price between $22 and $23 each, Goldman said.</p>
<p>IPO analysts have said that there is very high demand from large institutional investors for the IPO which could send the stock price soaring when it opens for trading tomorrow.</p>
</text>
